From: MediaBox
Subject: log to stderr, because fd 1 in a browser is not a terminal

This plugin writes its diagnostics with printf(), to stdout.

Inside Chromium that is not a terminal and not a log: a child process's fd 1 is
a socket the browser hands it, and on this appliance it is the mojo channel the
GPU process talks to the browser over. Every line the plugin prints goes into
that channel and is never seen.

Measured on RK3588: with the decoder failing on its first frame and the log
level turned all the way up -- from the environment and then, when that was not
believed, from the device file itself, which this plugin also reads it from --
not one line appeared anywhere, while /proc/<gpu>/fd showed `1 -> socket:[...]`
and `2 -> /tmp/chromium.log`. The plugin was running the whole time. Hours can
be spent on a decoder that is talking, into the one file descriptor nobody is
reading.

stderr is where a library's diagnostics belong, it is the descriptor Chromium
leaves alone, and it is not carrying anyone's protocol.
--- a/include/libv4l-rkmpp.h
+++ b/include/libv4l-rkmpp.h
@@ -67,10 +67,10 @@
 #define LOG(fmt, ...) do { \
 	struct timeval tv; \
 	gettimeofday(&tv, NULL); \
-	printf("[%03ld.%03ld] [RKMPP] [%ld] %s(%d): " fmt, \
-	       tv.tv_sec % 1000, tv.tv_usec / 1000, gettid(), \
-	       __func__, __LINE__, ##__VA_ARGS__); \
-	fflush(stdout); \
+	fprintf(stderr, "[%03ld.%03ld] [RKMPP] [%ld] %s(%d): " fmt, \
+	        tv.tv_sec % 1000, tv.tv_usec / 1000, gettid(), \
+	        __func__, __LINE__, ##__VA_ARGS__); \
+	fflush(stderr); \
 	} while (0)
 
 #define LOGV(level, fmt, ...) \
